course: dictionary
lesson: 10369
title: Treacle: a word with two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Treacle is a thick, sticky, dark sweet syrup. It is made when sugar is refined, which means it is cleaned and processed. «They live at the bottom of a well and eat nothing but treacle.» Eat nothing but treacle tells you it is a food, and a sweet, sticky one.
explain: Treacle can also mean something too sweet or soppy, like a speech full of sugary feelings. To tell which meaning is in use, read the words around it. Does the sentence talk about eating, baking or cooking? Then it means the syrup. Does it talk about a speech or a feeling that is too sweet? Then it means the second meaning.
fact: Treacle is a noun. In British English it is a thick, sticky, dark sweet syrup.
fact: Black treacle is very dark, and golden syrup is a lighter kind of treacle.
fact: In America, treacle is called molasses.
fact: Treacle is used in baking: treacle tart, gingerbread, parkin and sticky toffee pudding.
fact: «As slow as treacle» means moving very slowly.
exercise: «They live at the bottom of a well and eat nothing but treacle.» What is treacle? | A cold drink made from water and ice | A small flying insect | A kind of stone found in wells | *A thick, sticky, dark sweet syrup
exercise: «Her speech was pure treacle, full of sugary words about how wonderful everyone was.» What does treacle mean here? | A type of rain | Dark, sticky syrup for baking | *Something too sweet and soppy | A dish of hot custard
exercise: Which kind of treacle is the light kind? | Toffee | Gingerbread | *Golden syrup | Black treacle
test: Which of these is a dessert that uses treacle? | Fish fingers | Cheese sandwich | *Treacle tart | Boiled egg
test: Which phrase means moving very slowly? | Light as a feather | *As slow as treacle | Loud as a drum | Quick as a flash
exam: What do Americans call treacle? | Custard | Jam | *Molasses | Icing
